  "questions": [
    "Step 0's fixed rule says stop. Only PCA-10 (min 0.875) of FA-20 / PCA-10 / PCA-50 / scVI-10 has OT-flow-J fork AUC >= 0.85 on every seed; PCA-50 (min 0.559), scVI-10 (min 0.310) and FA-20 (min 0.043) do not. The FA-whitened OT cost raises FA to 0.21-0.97, not >= 0.85 on every seed. How should the workstream proceed: stop here as the rule says, or another task?"
  ],
  "observations": [
    "S10's OT velocity was reproduced exactly (max |dv| = 0), and the refitted OT flow J gives the same AUC to 4 decimals on all 12 PCA-20/FA-20 units.",
    "PCA-20 itself is below 0.85 on v3_transition s0 (0.818).",
    "OT-flow-J fork AUC is not monotone in PCA dimension: PCA-10 0.875-0.997, PCA-20 0.818-0.999, PCA-50 0.559-0.968. PCA-50 falls on v3_default s0 (0.637) and s2 (0.559) but not s1 (0.968).",
    "scVI-10: AUC 0.72-0.96 on v3_default and 0.31-0.56 on v3_transition. On v3_transition the leading eigenvector at saddle cells aligns poorly with the fate axis (|cos| 0.17-0.53).",
    "FA-20: OT velocities agree in sign with PCA-20 in gene space (cos > 0 for >= 99.9 % of cells), but only moderately in direction (median cos 0.52-0.56). The MeasuredDrift-fitted velocities agree less on v3_transition (median cos 0.09-0.28 over all cells).",
    "In FA-20 the committed cells sit about 1 unit from the saddle midpoint along the fate axis, vs 7-11 units in PCA-20. FA scores have about unit variance per axis; the median OT speed is 0.05-0.10 (FA) vs 0.17-0.28 (PCA-20).",
    "The whitened FA cost raises the FA AUC on every dataset (+0.15 to +0.85) and raises the fate-axis |cos| at saddles to 0.64-0.97, but it stays below 0.85 on 4 of 6 datasets.",
    "Restricting J to the top-5 local covariance directions does not remove the FA inversion (FA tangent-lambda1 AUC 0.09-0.61)."
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    "Since PCA-10 and PCA-20 pass while PCA-50 and scVI-10 do not, a sweep of PCA dimension (e.g. 5-50) on the development data would show where OT flow J stops resolving the fork. Its result is bounded by the S10 choice of 20.",
    "FA's committed/saddle separation along the fate axis is about 10x smaller than PCA's relative to its noise. A diagnostic that rescales FA axes (e.g. by the per-axis posterior precision) before OT and MeasuredDrift would test whether the inversion is a scale/regularisation effect of MeasuredDrift (weight decay) rather than of OT.",
    "The 22-29 saddle cells per v3_default seed make its AUCs noisy; v3_transition (350-368 saddle cells) is the more informative fork set."
